became free at 15.

00:10:53.519 --> 00:10:55.187 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, I mean, it's
hard to believe.

00:10:55.187 --> 00:10:56.689
So how many people were you with

00:10:56.689 --> 00:10:58.424
when you were crossing the Gobi?

00:10:58.424 --> 00:11:00.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
- We're like seven, eight,
and we had one baby,

00:11:00.826 --> 00:11:02.628
like two three years
old to ride with us.

00:11:02.628 --> 00:11:05.498 align:start size:88% position:13%
- And you had a compass
and the North star

00:11:05.498 --> 00:11:08.000 align:start size:81% position:19%
how long did it
take you to cross?

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.635 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It took us
several days journey

00:11:09.635 --> 00:11:11.871 align:start size:81% position:19%
to go to in the
Mongolia in china,

00:11:11.871 --> 00:11:14.840 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then from the night,
it was just one day.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:18.144 align:start size:88% position:13%
But we chose the
coldest time in February

00:11:18.144 --> 00:11:22.081 align:start size:97% position:3%
because during the summer
time is so literally watched

00:11:22.081 --> 00:11:23.582
they can just shoot us.

00:11:23.582 --> 00:11:25.084 align:start size:88% position:13%
But you know, in
February, normally think

00:11:25.084 --> 00:11:27.420
like somebody should to be
crazy enough to cross desert

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:29.188
in like minus 40 degrees.

00:11:29.188 --> 00:11:31.490
- Yeah, did you think that
you weren't gonna survive?

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:33.559 align:start size:81% position:19%
I mean, were there
moments where.

00:11:33.559 --> 00:11:36.929
- Yeah, I was, I like, I
remember still remember

00:11:36.929 --> 00:11:39.098
standing on the desert, like

00:11:39.098 --> 00:11:41.734 align:start size:84% position:16%
I felt completely
alone in this world.

00:11:41.734 --> 00:11:45.271
We normally would have known
if I stay on the desert. Right.

00:11:45.271 --> 00:11:48.507
And that's what I felt
like so many people dying

00:11:48.507 --> 00:11:49.809
without like,

00:11:49.809 --> 00:11:52.611
even more knowing about
it completely invisible.

00:11:52.611 --> 00:11:54.213
And I just thought like

00:11:54.213 --> 00:11:56.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
what scared me most was
not even dying that night.

00:11:56.849 --> 00:11:58.117
It was just like,

00:11:58.117 --> 00:12:00.119
no one gonna knew that
I existed in this world.

00:12:01.387 --> 00:12:02.988 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well, they definitely
know you exist now.

00:12:02.988 --> 00:12:05.357
So you, when you got to Mongolia

00:12:05.357 --> 00:12:08.127
what did you have to
give people to trade

00:12:08.127 --> 00:12:10.563 align:start size:97% position:3%
so that they would help you
get to South Korea from there?

00:12:10.563 --> 00:12:12.998
What's in it for
them at that point?

00:12:12.998 --> 00:12:15.634
- Yeah, so Mongolia has
some kind of theory with

00:12:15.634 --> 00:12:17.069
South Korea.

00:12:17.069 --> 00:12:20.539 align:start size:97% position:3%
And as soon as we got
caught by Mongolian soldier

00:12:20.539 --> 00:12:23.109
and they were like using
guns trying to shoot us.

00:12:23.109 --> 00:12:25.478 align:start size:88% position:13%
And the thing first
thing was doing to them.

00:12:25.478 --> 00:12:26.946
Like I was thanking them

00:12:26.946 --> 00:12:29.815 align:start size:97% position:3%
because I could have been
just easily lost in the desert

00:12:29.815 --> 00:12:33.185 align:start position:0%
and no one could have found
us, at least soldier, found us.

00:12:33.185 --> 00:12:35.654
And they were of course,
trying to send us back

00:12:35.654 --> 00:12:38.424 align:start size:84% position:16%
to China and then
some back North Korea.

00:12:38.424 --> 00:12:39.992
But when North (indistinct)

00:12:39.992 --> 00:12:41.894
when they escape, they are like

00:12:41.894 --> 00:12:45.464
during the Holocaust
Jews brought us like
poisons with them.

00:12:45.464 --> 00:12:46.665
That's what we do.

00:12:46.665 --> 00:12:49.335
We bring lasers and
poisons with us.

00:12:49.335 --> 00:12:50.803
And if we called them back

00:12:50.803 --> 00:12:52.104 align:start size:81% position:19%
we were gonna just
kill ourselves

00:12:52.104 --> 00:12:54.840
before we go through
all of that journey.

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:57.009
And they were trying
send us back to China.

00:12:57.009 --> 00:12:59.578 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then we were trying
to take the poisons

00:12:59.578 --> 00:13:00.846
and to kill all ourselves.

00:13:00.846 --> 00:13:04.150
And they took a pity
on us and they actually

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:07.987 align:start size:97% position:3%
contacted South Korea instead
of the North Korean one.

00:13:07.987 --> 00:13:11.590
And they have dust to go
to South Korea as refugee.

00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:13.859
- All right.

00:13:13.859 --> 00:13:15.127
Well, since I know
from hanging out

00:13:15.127 --> 00:13:17.496
with you for a couple of
years, a couple of hours

00:13:17.496 --> 00:13:20.566
I should say, I know what
a nice smile you have.

00:13:20.566 --> 00:13:22.067
So let's get,

00:13:22.067 --> 00:13:24.737
to the part where this starts
turning into a happy story.

00:13:24.737 --> 00:13:26.205
- Yeah

00:13:26.205 --> 00:13:29.542 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So now you end up in South
Korea and what happens?

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:34.880
- I'm learning how
freedom is so hard.

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:38.117
It was very difficult to be free

00:13:38.117 --> 00:13:42.221
because in North Korea, like
everything was decided for me.

00:13:42.221 --> 00:13:44.924
Government's telling me what
to wear, what to listen to,

00:13:44.924 --> 00:13:48.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
what to watch and so in
South Korea, they say like

00:13:48.394 --> 00:13:49.929
what do you think?

00:13:49.929 --> 00:13:51.797
And I was only wondering why
does it matter what I think

00:13:51.797 --> 00:13:53.732
just tell me what to do.

00:13:53.732 --> 00:13:56.035
And they said, what do
you wanna be? It's like,

00:13:56.035 --> 00:13:58.037
so the fact that in South Korea

00:13:58.037 --> 00:14:00.973 align:start size:88% position:13%
I had to be responsible
for my choices

00:14:00.973 --> 00:14:03.075 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is so hard to
adapt in the beginning

00:14:03.075 --> 00:14:04.276
coming from North Korea.

00:14:04.276 --> 00:14:05.945
And I was thinking like

00:14:05.945 --> 00:14:08.214 align:start size:84% position:16%
if someone guaranteed
my life safety,

00:14:08.214 --> 00:14:10.916 align:start size:97% position:3%
I will do this go back North
Korea and be slave again.

00:14:10.916 --> 00:14:15.187 align:start size:97% position:3%
That's how hard transitioning
was coming from, you know

00:14:15.187 --> 00:14:17.089
North Korea to free world.

00:14:17.089 --> 00:14:18.591
- How do you make that switch.

00:14:19.458 --> 00:14:20.960
its mentally

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.428
- Books really helped me.

00:14:22.428 --> 00:14:26.599 align:start size:97% position:3%
I was starting reading Georgia
West animal farm in 1984.

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:29.001
But to that point, you know

00:14:29.001 --> 00:14:31.103 align:start size:84% position:16%
when I was arriving
in South Korea,

00:14:31.103 --> 00:14:33.873
people were telling me
like Kings or dictators

00:14:33.873 --> 00:14:35.908
and you were lied, you know

00:14:35.908 --> 00:14:38.577
everything you learned
in North Korea was lie

00:14:38.577 --> 00:14:40.980
Americans are not pastors.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:43.649
And you know, they're
like Japanese are not.

00:14:43.649 --> 00:14:45.117
And they're like

00:14:45.117 --> 00:14:46.919 align:start size:97% position:3%
they keep telling me the
good things about the world.

00:14:46.919 --> 00:14:48.721
And by that point, I was like

00:14:48.721 --> 00:14:51.590
completely lost my
faith in humanity.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:53.092
I was thinking, so like

00:14:53.092 --> 00:14:55.828 align:start size:97% position:3%
if everything that I believe
in North Korea was a lie.

00:14:55.828 --> 00:14:58.097
How do I know what you
are saying is not lying

00:14:58.097 --> 00:14:59.598
- Yeah

00:14:59.598 --> 00:15:02.034
- Was really hard
to believe again.

00:15:02.034 --> 00:15:03.302
- How do you get over that.

00:15:03.302 --> 00:15:05.437
I mean, that must be,
I'm guessing the scars

00:15:05.437 --> 00:15:08.240
of that have to be with
you right now still.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:11.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
- No, Georgia while
reading his book was just

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:12.645
made complete sense.

00:15:12.645 --> 00:15:16.115 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like I could see in that
little pigs in the animal farm

00:15:16.115 --> 00:15:19.084
was it, I see myself as in
my grandmother's like, Oh

00:15:19.084 --> 00:15:20.819
this is what happened.

00:15:20.819 --> 00:15:24.023 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so I became really good
friends with the books.

00:15:24.023 --> 00:15:26.892
And of course I've been
so inspired in your book

00:15:26.892 --> 00:15:28.227
don't burn this world.

00:15:28.227 --> 00:15:29.528
And

00:15:29.528 --> 00:15:30.963
- That was years later.

00:15:30.963 --> 00:15:33.132
You were already on your way

00:15:33.132 --> 00:15:35.134
by the time you read my book.

00:15:36.335 --> 00:15:38.504
So then what did you start doing

00:15:38.504 --> 00:15:41.774
in South Korea that started
getting you some notoriety

00:15:41.774 --> 00:15:43.242
and people started
knowing who you were

00:15:43.242 --> 00:15:46.178
and then in 2014 and it
seems like that's where

00:15:46.178 --> 00:15:49.381
things really started to catch
on at an international level.

00:15:50.849 --> 00:15:53.252
- So in South Korea never
planned to be an activist

00:15:53.252 --> 00:15:54.520
or none of that,

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:58.090
but I lost my sister,
as I said, I lost her.

00:15:58.090 --> 00:16:00.359
She escaped me when she was 16.

00:16:00.359 --> 00:16:01.627
And then I was 13 and we

00:16:01.627 --> 00:16:04.863 align:start size:84% position:16%
I didn't see her
for like, from 2007.

00:16:04.863 --> 00:16:07.599
So I realized in order to
find that I need to get

00:16:07.599 --> 00:16:11.437 align:start size:97% position:3%
on like the news sort of
broadcast to find her somehow.

00:16:11.437 --> 00:16:13.372
So I started joining a TV shows

00:16:13.372 --> 00:16:16.008
in South Korea and
looking for her.

00:16:16.008 --> 00:16:19.745 align:start size:88% position:13%
And that like really led
me to activism later.

00:16:19.745 --> 00:16:23.983 align:start position:0%
And yeah, but I found my sister
though, seven years later.

00:16:23.983 --> 00:16:25.351
So it paid off.

00:16:25.351 --> 00:16:27.086
- Yeah, what was that like?

00:16:27.086 --> 00:16:28.520 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, it sounds like
such a ridiculous question.

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:29.888
What was that like? But.

00:16:31.323 --> 00:16:33.993
- I mean, she is the only
living family that I got

00:16:33.993 --> 00:16:35.494
from all of this.

00:16:35.494 --> 00:16:38.497
Like, because of my spoke
out against the dictator

00:16:38.497 --> 00:16:41.834
all my three generations of
my family back in North Korea

00:16:41.834 --> 00:16:43.769
being sent to prison camp

00:16:43.769 --> 00:16:46.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
or being executed
because I'm speaking out.

00:16:46.705 --> 00:16:49.308
So I'm not still free
from the dictator.

00:16:49.308 --> 00:16:50.609
There are still consequences

00:16:50.609 --> 00:16:53.512
for me having a voice
and she was alive.

00:16:53.512 --> 00:16:56.281
She was the only one that
I got from all of this.

00:16:56.281 --> 00:16:57.516
- Yeah.

00:16:57.516 --> 00:16:59.518 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then how were
you sort of welcomed

00:16:59.518 --> 00:17:02.788
into the Western
world after this?

00:17:02.788 --> 00:17:05.924
I mean, now you live in
Chicago now your friends.

00:17:05.924 --> 00:17:07.593
We have a ton of similar friends

00:17:07.593 --> 00:17:09.661 align:start size:84% position:16%
that are all fighting
these battles,

00:17:09.661 --> 00:17:11.964 align:start size:84% position:16%
but you've lived
through this battle.

00:17:11.964 --> 00:17:15.167
How did, you go from
just sort of activism

00:17:15.167 --> 00:17:17.669
in South Korea to
where you are now?

00:17:18.804 --> 00:17:20.572
- Yeah, in South Korea,
unfortunately I was,

00:17:20.572 --> 00:17:24.176
heavily discriminated
and I couldn't fit in.

00:17:24.176 --> 00:17:27.112
I had to lie to people
that I was South Korean

00:17:27.112 --> 00:17:30.082 align:start size:97% position:3%
'cause they were not so many
things like South Koreans

00:17:30.082 --> 00:17:33.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
who were discriminated
against for North Koreans.

00:17:33.285 --> 00:17:35.120 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's why I chose
to come to America.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.890 align:start size:97% position:3%
Even the people who say
this is like racist country.

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:41.493
This is a country I have been
where most embracing included

00:17:41.493 --> 00:17:42.728
in my life.

00:17:42.728 --> 00:17:45.330
So I chose U.S as my
home cause it's like,

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:47.733
there's no racism for
me here to experience.

00:17:47.733 --> 00:17:50.936 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Right before we
get to the non-racism

00:17:50.936 --> 00:17:52.571
of the United States.

00:17:52.571 --> 00:17:55.541 align:start size:84% position:16%
So, South Koreans
were discriminating
against North Koreans.

00:17:55.541 --> 00:17:58.143 align:start size:88% position:13%
Was that, simply
because they didn't know

00:17:58.143 --> 00:17:59.611
North Koreans or they
felt that too many

00:17:59.611 --> 00:18:02.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
North Koreans were coming
over or what is that?

00:18:02.047 --> 00:18:03.282
'cause you don't really think

00:18:03.282 --> 00:18:05.818
that there would be that
type of discrimination

00:18:05.818 --> 00:18:08.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Just because we are
coming from a poor country

00:18:08.887 --> 00:18:12.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you know, South
Koreans, they discriminate

00:18:12.091 --> 00:18:15.360 align:start size:97% position:3%
against like Southeast Asians,
like Vietnamese, Thailand,

00:18:16.762 --> 00:18:19.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
Filipinos and North Korea
is also poor country.

00:18:19.631 --> 00:18:21.600 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't think they
discriminate people as much

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:24.736
when they come from
France or Europe,

00:18:24.736 --> 00:18:26.672
Western Europe, or like USA,

00:18:26.672 --> 00:18:29.675
but do that when people
coming from poor country.

00:18:29.675 --> 00:18:33.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, even though we were
saying people, when I went

00:18:33.178 --> 00:18:36.482 align:start size:97% position:3%
to South Korea, they were
just making fun of my accent

00:18:36.482 --> 00:18:39.618
'cause I was speaking with
Northern accent and, you know

00:18:39.618 --> 00:18:41.653
they were asking me
like, are you a spy

00:18:41.653 --> 00:18:43.088
why are you talking to me?

00:18:43.088 --> 00:18:47.993 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it's like, if I were
spy, why would I even escape?

00:18:47.993 --> 00:18:50.496
So it was very tough.

00:18:50.496 --> 00:18:51.964
- Right.

00:18:51.964 --> 00:18:54.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
So what put you on my
radar was a few months ago

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:57.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
a whole bunch of people
started sending me a video

00:18:57.302 --> 00:18:58.770
of you talking about

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:00.772 align:start size:97% position:3%
your adventure and your
journey and everything else.

00:19:00.772 --> 00:19:03.809 align:start size:84% position:16%
And you happen to
mention that you read

00:19:03.809 --> 00:19:05.077
"don't burn this book"

00:19:05.077 --> 00:19:07.679
and that it helped you
in some way, which is

00:19:07.679 --> 00:19:09.248
I don't even have the words

00:19:09.248 --> 00:19:11.550 align:start size:84% position:16%
to explain my
gratitude for that.

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:12.484
I mean,

00:19:12.484 --> 00:19:13.652
it's just beyond imagination

00:19:13.652 --> 00:19:15.254 align:start size:84% position:16%
considering what
you've lived through.

00:19:15.254 --> 00:19:18.657
But in essence, you are now
here in the United States.

00:19:18.657 --> 00:19:20.659 align:start size:88% position:13%
Do you consider yourself
an activist first?

00:19:20.659 --> 00:19:22.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like what do you consider
yourself now? Really.

00:19:22.961 --> 00:19:24.396
You're an author obviously.

00:19:24.396 --> 00:19:25.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you're out there
fighting all these battles

00:19:25.998 --> 00:19:27.799 align:start size:84% position:16%
but what do you
consider yourself now.

00:19:27.799 --> 00:19:29.735
- I'm a fighter,

00:19:29.735 --> 00:19:33.205 align:start size:97% position:3%
and am trying to fight against
North Korean dictatorship

00:19:33.205 --> 00:19:36.241
and Chinese communist party
that sponsors dictatorship

00:19:36.241 --> 00:19:37.843
in North Korea.

00:19:37.843 --> 00:19:40.479
And I think that's why I began.

00:19:40.479 --> 00:19:43.615 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, on chair, I read
your book and it was

00:19:43.615 --> 00:19:47.052
I was more trying to
be, you know, what

00:19:47.052 --> 00:19:49.521 align:start size:84% position:16%
like try to do my best
to raise awareness.

00:19:49.521 --> 00:19:52.057
And at Hollywood, everybody

00:19:52.057 --> 00:19:54.159
they don't pick up
North Korean story.

00:19:54.159 --> 00:19:55.594
Like they talk about slavery

00:19:55.594 --> 00:19:59.198 align:start position:0%
and they talk about like
Malala, who was shot by Taliban.

00:19:59.198 --> 00:20:02.067
They talk about what
was captured by ISIS,

00:20:02.067 --> 00:20:04.903 align:start size:97% position:3%
and Michelle Obama with
standing up alcohol anchors

00:20:04.903 --> 00:20:07.206
or these people in the
mainstream standing up

00:20:07.206 --> 00:20:10.108
for a lot of girls and like
human trafficking issues.

00:20:10.108 --> 00:20:12.811 align:start size:88% position:13%
But nobody here in
like West wants to talk

00:20:12.811 --> 00:20:14.012
about North Korea

00:20:14.012 --> 00:20:16.481 align:start size:84% position:16%
because that offsets
Chinese regime.

00:20:17.583 --> 00:20:18.517
- Is it?

00:20:18.517 --> 00:20:19.985
Yeah, Is that crazy for you?

00:20:19.985 --> 00:20:23.355
Like you come here and you see

00:20:23.355 --> 00:20:26.925 align:start size:84% position:16%
this sort of fear
around talking, not
just about North Korea

00:20:26.925 --> 00:20:28.627
but we talked about
this a little bit

00:20:28.627 --> 00:20:29.561
a couple of weeks ago.

00:20:29.561 --> 00:20:30.629
just that you see the way

00:20:30.629 --> 00:20:32.965
we are afraid of
speaking up here

00:20:32.965 --> 00:20:34.366 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the freest
country in the world

00:20:34.366 --> 00:20:36.501
about whatever it might be.

00:20:36.501 --> 00:20:39.071 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, I mean, that's like,
that's so shocking to me.

00:20:39.071 --> 00:20:41.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought America
was like land of the free

00:20:41.807 --> 00:20:43.775
the home of the brave way.

